sevillad@gmail.com <sevillad@gmail.com> kirjoitti 27.02.2007:
> 
> ...  I've read the spoilers, I'd like to know if I'd be doing
> something stupid by diluting any of these potions (maybe some of
> them are important):
>
> blindness, booze, fruit

Dilute.

> healing, gain energy

Save for alchemy, or quaff to raise your stats.

> hallu

Dilute.

> invisibility

If not permanently invisible yet, bless and quaff one.  If you have no
holy water yet, you may want to keep an unblessed one until you find a
stalker corpse and quaff it before eating.  If already permanently
invisible, dilute.

> levitation (I expect a ring someday)

Keep until you get that ring (or boots or spell).  Somewhat useful for
alchemy, so may be worth saving anyway.

> monster&object detection

Save if you think you have use for these, else dilute.  Monster
detection may worth saving if you don't have telepathy and a blindfold
or towel yet.  Object detection is useful enough, but also very common
(since nymphs often carry them), and doesn't really give you all that
much except convenience.  Both become mostly obsolete once (if) you
learn the corresponding spells.  I dilute them, but YMMV.

> oil

Save if you don't have a magic lamp (or the PYEC).  Else dilute.

> paralysis

This can be used offensively, particularly if you have free action.
Might be worth saving.  Then again, might not, particularly if you
have many.

> restore ability

Dilute, at least if you already have a unicorn horn.

> see invisible

Bless and quaff one if you don't have the permanent intrinsic yet.
Else dilute.  Note that eating a stalker while invisible gives you
both invisibility and see invisible as permanent intrinsics.

> sickness

Could be useful for poisoning (some) weapons, or for throwing the
potions themselves.  As a lawful Valk I dilute these, as a neutral
Healer I keep them.  Save as many as you think you'll use, dilute the
rest.

> sleeping

Same as paralysis.

> speed (I expect boots)

Keep for alchemy -- or for escape until you get the boots (or the
spell), particularly if you're not intrinsically fast yet.

> These I'd keep:
>
> - FHeal,XHeal: i'd use them for MAX HP.

Good choice.  Bless and alchemize for maximum effect.  Note that full
healing can be alchemized to gain ability, which, blessed, allows you
to max your stats (always a desirable goal).

> - Conf: I've read that sometimes it's good to be confused to read/
> drink certain things.

An expired spell will work almost as well, and is always available.
Once you have one, the potions are much less useful.  They do have
some rather limited use in alchemy, but I generally find them best
diluted once I no longer need them.

> - Enligh: Blessed are good to raise stats.

Also somewhat useful for alchemy, and also for, well, enlightenment.

> - Gain ability, gain level.

Gain ability is pretty useless (though still better than _restore_
ability) once your stats (other than STR) are maxed.  Until then,
bless and quaff.  Gain level and gain energy are not only good when
blessed and quaffed, but are also essential ingredients for alchemy.
Cursed gain level also has its uses.

> - Polymorph: may not be useful, but looks so unpredictable it must be
> fun! (maybe a YASD will convince me soon...)

Perhaps best saved for emergencies, or for strategic use once you have
polycontrol.  Has a number of uses, though most are risky, at least if
not controlled.

> Other questions:
>
> When can I use a u. horn to recover lost stats? Does it have to be in
> the turn after losing them? I'm asking because sometimes I may need to
> run away from a monster in order not to be hit again while (a) it!

As already noted, any time.  The game keeps track of what your maximum
stats were.  (Note that there _are_ some things, like, IIRC, turning
into a new man/woman when polymorphing, which can reset these values.)

> Is it important to bless my horn? I'll do it eventually but I'd like
> to know if it's a priority.

It's not the single most urgent thing to bless, but certainly among
the few most important ones.  Once you've got your BoH and luckstone
blessed, I'd do the unihorn next.  Other important things to bless are
magic lamps and smoky potions, if any, and a touchstone if you're not
a gnome or an Arch.  And various scrolls and potions, of course.

Anyway, once you've diluted and blessed all those spare potions, you
should have enough holy water to bless everything you need and still
have several to spare.

> Do I exercise daggers skill by throwing them? I've been doing it for a
> while and I got nothing, the minute I wielded one and used it I got an
> enhancement...

Assuming you hit and do damage, yes.

> I got an uncursed scroll of genocide... being a Val, is there anything
> particularly nasty to save it for? If I have a hard monster hitting me
> is that a good moment to read it and kill him? At this point (Lvl 11,
> HP=112) shall I consider going to Sokoban and nurse dancing?

Saving it until you need it is a good strategy.  Think of it as a "get
out of trouble free" card.

Even once you get several, don't get too carried away with them.  The
more monsters you genocide, the more common the rest become, and the
really hard ones aren't genocidable anyway.  Most of the dangerous
monsters in nethack are also useful in some way: mind flayers are good
eating, cockatrice corpses (and eggs) make great weapons, etc.  Even
liches have their uses, if you, say, want to get an athame the hard
way.  Just about the only completely useless monster I can think of
are green slimes, and I'm sure someone could find a use even for them.

For reverse genociding, another good choice besides nurses would be
wraiths.  Just make sure you're protected from their attacks; for
lawful characters, wielding Excalibur works nicely.  Oh, and don't be
satiated.

Despite what some spoilers might claim, foocubi are not genocidable,
and therefore can't be reverse genocided either.  Sorry.

